t hill  the secured area includes almost 100  checkpoints that will have police  presence to ensure that those seeking  entry to that secure area for a unlawful  reason such as joining a proto protest  cannot enter the downtown core  again i know that these are measures  that our community is not used to  they will be in place only as long as  necessary to un remove the unlawful  protests  our officers are aware of the impact on  you and we're taking every step we can  to minimize the impact on our residents  and businesses while keeping out those  who could do more harm to our community  we want to reassure everyone that if you  live work or have a lawful reason to be  in the area there will be minimal  impacts on your access  once through the checkpoints those with  a lawful reason will be free to move  about individuals may leave the secure  area at any time  as we continue to increase our actions  we will be communicating them directly  to the public we have open lines of  communication with our schools and other  institutions in the area  to those engaged in the unlawful protest  if you want to leave under your own  terms now is the time to do it  i'm available to take questions thank  you  and i'll invite each media to come to  the microphone  and ask a question please when you  search the question start with your name  and the media you represent  is  hello chief natalie van roy from ctv  ottawa are ottawa police asking  businesses  near the red zone to stay closed for an  extended period of time  so as i indicated so thank you first  thank you very much for the question  as i indicated we've developed this  secure area where people who live work  or have lawful reasons to be there are  free to come and go we're just  restricting the area from people who  have come in over the past number of  weeks particularly on the weekends as  we're getting towards to be engaged in  unlawful activity we have several  officers in the area both on foot and in  vehicles to ensure the safety and  security of the neighborhoods and the  areas that surround  where the prosta protest footprint is  what measures are being considered if  protesters do not comply if they do not  leave that secure area  so we've been really clear with everyone  since the very beginning this is it's  time to go your time in our city has  come to an end and you must leave we've  engaged in interactions with the  protesters to to attempt to  persuade negotiate with them to leave  the footprint of our area we will  continue to do that but what i can tell  you is we have a deliberate plan of  action to take in order to make sure  that our streets are turned back to our  residents and our community is turned  back to normal  hi elizabeth laplante i'm from tva news  in montreal when are you planning to  intervene  for the kids  in the protest  so thanks for the question one of the  key concerns that we've had as we've  planned and and looked at how we want to  proceed to end this protest is the  number of children that remain in there  we continue to work with our partners  from the children's aid society and  other social services to look at the  best most safest way to have children  removed from the area  prior to any sort of police action we've  had members of our police service  continue to engage with the protesters  to identify that it is not a good place  for children to be that they should make  every attempt to remove children from  the area all of our planning has been  very considerate of the people that are  within the demonstration zone including  the children will they be the first to  be removed as i indicated we've worked  really hard to make sure all of our  plans are very deliberate around  protecting children that may be in that  footprint  mr bell mackenzie gray with cdb national  news to be frank it's been 21 days now  and the residents of this city have been  pretty clear that the police in the city  have completely bungled dealing with  this protest it's not the first time  we've had a press conference here from  the police saying there's a new plan to  deal with it so why should any of the  residents of the city believe that this  time is going to be different  so thank you for the question um  i think you just need to go outside and  look at the presence we have right now  we're taking unprecedented steps through  support of both federal provincial  legislation  municipal increase in in fines for  bylaws as well as injunctions to bring  all that together to work with our  partners from the opp and rcmp to amass  a plan and amass the resources we need  to actually execute that plan as you're  seeing in the occurrence that's happened  the activity that's happened with police  over the last day and a half or so  you're seeing a much increased presence  of officers that is to indicate that we  are at the end of this protest we will  take what action we need to deliberately  safely lawfully end these demonstrations  i'm happy you mentioned going outside  because if you walked on wellington  street right now there are two guys in a  hot tub and there's a bouncy castle  across from them can you assure the  residents of the city that this will no  longer happen and that the parties that  have happened on wellington street for  the last three weekends will end this  week  that's what we're here to say today we  absolutely are committed to end this  unlawful demonstration we have the plan  we have the commitment we have the  resources and we have the amazing  partnership of all policing partners to  make sure that this unlawful  demonstration comes to an end  chief bell thanks for taking our  questions um you're talking about  setting up checkpoints making sure  people have a lawful reason to be going  downtown how are these going to work um  been seeing some reports that people are  just asking oh why are you going down  okay go ahead so what's going to be  stopping protesters from just lying and  saying they work downtown or they live  downtown  so as we indicated we have um over a  hundred checkpoints in this secure area  that we've established officers are  continuing to be informed um of uh the  the lawful reasons why how they can stop  and challenge people and then looking to  ensure that people are entering the area  who live there who work there or who  have a lawful reason such as a medical  appointment to attend there our officers  have that information and are  intervening on people who are not  supposed to be there stopping them and  allowing people that should be there  their lawful right to move around in  those areas  yeah and just on the difficulty of  dealing with children in the protest  we my colleagues have been speaking to  some people out there right now who have  kids are saying it's a completely safe  place they don't plan on leaving anytime  soon and encouraging other families to  bring their kids out there  just how did the police navigate the  situation with child with a children's  aid if people aren't going to be leaving  the police plan on coming in and  separating families  so as as i indicated earlier we continue  to work with the children's aid society  and our planners to make sure that the  safety of any  children or youth that are in that area  in the footprint of the demonstration is  utmost in our priority as we look to  dismantle this demonstration  chief bell john willing with the citizen  do you have a goal in terms of how many  trucks you want to remove from the core  daily or even by the end of this long  weekend  so we won't be establishing any goals or  targets what i can tell you is we we are  continuing to to dialogue discuss with  protesters in there uh identifying that  it is time for them to go that this is  coming to an end and that we will  continue to increase our actions until  ultimately everyone is gone from that  area that area is returned to the  citizens of ottawa and we have normalcy  in the downtown core thank you have you  secured heavy tow availability for the  next few days we we continue to work uh  on our plans we've developed all those  plans and we aren't seeing any issues  with the ability to remove vehicles at  this point  um has you felt it's a joint canelo from  cbc news a little bit on that same theme  he said earlier it's going to be  methodical it's going to take time  can you give us a sense about of how  much time you think it will take and you  know we're on to a weekend number four  are you expecting  more people in the demonstrator  reinforcements as you say to come back  like what do you see happening over the  next little while so thank you for the  question um what i can tell you is the  steps the deliberate steps we've taken  to create the secure zone under the  powers that have been granted to us  under the federal emergencies act are  directly aligned to make sure that we  don't see the numbers in the  demonstration bolstered over the weekend  we have an a very deliberate plan that  will be methodical and will take time  for us to progress through to be able to  completely remove anyone from the core  so what i can tell you is this weekend  will look very different than the past  three weekends and for people who like  have kids who are coming to school here  you know there's a high school nearby  there's a public school maybe offices  are you asking people not to come  tomorrow what you know there's concerns  about from parents as you can imagine  so i can absolutely i can absolutely  understand that there's concerns from  all pockets of our community about  what's going on  we continue to work with institutions  like the school boards to identify any  sort of concerns that may exist within  the footprint and we'll continue to  provide public safety or media through  media advisories to all of our community  to let them know what's happening how we  progress and if we have any immediate or  emerging safety concerns that people  need to know about  hi chief laura osmond the canadian press  i'm just wondering how critical the  emergencies act powers that have been  granted to you by the federal government  are in terms of your plan is this  something you would have been able to do  without that legislation invoked  so thanks it's a great question  what i can tell you is we've seen a  growing frustration within our community  within the provincial government within  the federal government around the  activities that are occurring here  we've also seen the growth in our  authorities and ability to actually  successfully deal with the demonstration  unprecedented that unlawful  demonstration like we're seeing downtown  in our core  all of those legislation pieces of  legislation and supports we've got from  different levels of government have  directly and actively contributed to our  ability to ultimately say we are in a  position to move forward and look to end  this demonstration  of course downtown is not the only place  that these trucks have been amassing  there are encampments all over the city  more were popping up last weekend you  had to shut down  what assurances can you give people that  as you direct people away from the  downtown core over the long weekend as  people are trying to flood into ottawa  that it's not going to end up in their  communities  so  i would understand the concern about  that absolutely what i can tell you is  we've had great partnership through the  opp the rcmp other municipal police  agencies to make sure that we have  amassed the number of members officers  support functions in and around the  ottawa area to be able to make sure that  we not only demobilize the demonstration  that exists but that we look at  protecting ourselves against just  displacing it our goal is to take our  streets back our goal is to actually  give the streets of ottawa back to the  community that own it and deserve it we  will continue to do that while trying to  ensure ensuring that this doesn't  actually just displace to somewhere else  hi chief bell  frederick  so  you mentioned just earlier before that  you're still negotiating or speaking  with people that own the heavy vehicles  over there  so are you still at that point where  you're trying to get them to leave on  their own or you're past that point and  you know that you're gonna have to  intervene with force  so we'll never be past that point  i implore anyone that's there get in  your truck we will  navigate safe passage for you to leave  our city streets we want this to end  this demonstration to end peacefully we  want people to realize that it is coming  to an end and not  not require us to escalate in terms of  how we look to deal with demobilizing it  we will never stop trying to get people  to leave our streets that's exactly what  we want them to do just know that  there's a deliberate plan there's  commitment and there's the resourcing  that we now have in place to actually  finally end this but it can be ended by  all the demonstrators that sit there by  getting in their vehicles and going home  are you negotiating or in talks at all  with people that are  or say that they are at the head of this  convoy organizers per se are you  negotiating with them at all so as i  indicated we continue to negotiate with  individuals and with people that  represent different pockets within the  demonstration group it is our desire it  is in everyone's best interest it is  absolutely what we want to do is to have  this end peacefully we want people to go  home we will talk to anyone who we need  to talk to for them to go home but the  demonstrators there need to know we have  commitment we have a plan this needs to  end and you don't think that there's  going to be a fourth weekend of big  parties and celebration like just like  we've seen last weekend i can't place  any timelines on when it will ultimately  culminate i can tell you it will be a  very different picture in the downtown  core this weekend th